SUMMARY:Dinosaurs in Action: Green-Wood’s Birds of Prey 
DESCRIPTION:Green-Wood is one of the best places in New York City to spot birds of prey—and not just soaring overhead! Here\, you can witness raptors going about their daily lives: hunting and feeding\, courting and nesting\, learning to fly (a wobbly process!)\, and simply hanging out.  \n\n\n\nDrawing on years of observation and photography\, urban naturalist Matthew Wills will take you inside the fascinating world of Green-Wood’s raptors. Through a lively\, image-filled presentation\, you’ll discover the behaviors and lifestyles of these modern-day heirs of the theropod dinosaurs\, from daytime hunters like eagles\, hawks\, and falcons to the mysterious owls that emerge after dark.  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPrice: $25 / $20 for members  \n\n\n\n\nGet Tickets\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWalking Tour(see details below)\n\n\n\n\n\nBEFORE RESERVING YOUR SPOT\, PLEASE NOTE:\n\n\n\n\nTickets: There is no need to print tickets! Attendees will be checked in by name. \n\n\n\nWhere To Go: Check-in takes place at the Green-House\, near the Main Entrance at Fifth Avenue and 25th Street (750 Fifth Avenue). \n\n\n\nAccessibility & Safety: The Green-House is ADA-accessible. For disability-related accommodations\, contact us at 718-768-7300 ext. 5 or events@green-wood.com. 
URL:https://www.green-wood.com/event/dinosaurs-in-action-green-woods-birds-of-prey/
CATEGORIES:Walking Tour
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.green-wood.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/RTH.jpg
END:VEVENT
